Clackatoo
=========

Clackatoo is a modified version of HeliBoard.

Modifications notice (GPL-3.0 section 5a)
-----------------------------------------

This program is a modified version of HeliBoard v4.2
(https://github.com/HeliBorg/HeliBoard, tag v4.2), modified starting on
2026-10-20. The modifications are recorded in this repository's git history on
top of the upstream tag v4.2 (`git diff v4.2 main`). In summary:

- 2026-10-20: application id, labels and content provider authorities changed
  (now `io.github.highlyproteus.clackatoo` and "Clackatoo", see 2026-10-27).
- 2026-10-20: added the "Clackatoo" keyboard style (square keys with a thin
  border, Tokyo Night colours, JetBrains Mono key labels) and made it the
  default style and colour theme. New files: the package
  `helium314.keyboard.clackatoo`, `res/values/themes-clackatoo.xml`, a few
  `*_clackatoo` drawables, `assets/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf`. Small hooks
  were added to `KeyboardTheme`, `Colors`, `KeyboardTypeface`, `Defaults`, the
  appearance and colour settings screens, `SuggestionStripView` and
  `ClipboardHistoryManager`. HeliBoard's own styles and themes are unchanged.
- 2026-10-20: added offline voice typing (a Voice key on the toolbar: speech
  to text with whisper.cpp, English clean-up with S1-mini, text inserted at the
  cursor) and an offline grammar Check (a Check key on the toolbar: Qwen3.5
  0.8B proposes corrections that replace the checked text after the user
  accepts). New files: the package `helium314.keyboard.clackatoo.assist`, the
  `ml` Gradle module (JNI wrapper and build of whisper.cpp and llama.cpp),
  `res/values/strings-clackatoo-assist.xml`, `res/xml/backup_rules.xml`,
  `res/xml/data_extraction_rules.xml`, `assets/licenses/ml-notices.txt`,
  `settings/screens/AssistScreens.kt`, `ic_grammar_check.xml`. Small hooks were added to `LatinIME`,
  `KeyboardSwitcher`, `KeyboardActionListenerImpl`, `KeyboardWrapperView`,
  `App`, `ToolbarUtils`, `KeyCode`, `KeyboardIconsSet`, `InputAttributes`,
  `Defaults`, the settings navigation and main settings screen, and the
  manifest (the RECORD_AUDIO permission, an isolated model service and a
  permission activity). The app has no INTERNET permission.
- 2026-10-20: security hardening of voice typing and the grammar check after a
  review: the model service runs as an isolated process and receives models as
  file descriptors; model files are accepted only if they match the pinned size
  and SHA-256; model output is sanitised before it is shown or inserted; the
  grammar check replaces text only if the field is unchanged since it was read;
  the model folder is excluded from backup and device transfer; the
  open-source notices of whisper.cpp, llama.cpp and ggml are shown in the
  settings.
- 2026-10-20: second security round on voice typing and the grammar check:
  no build type loads a user-supplied native library any more (the "load
  gesture typing library" setting is removed from the settings screen); the
  grammar check reads a field that does not report where its text starts only
  if the selection matches the keyboard's own; invisible and format characters
  in model output are removed unless the user's text had them; the Check key,
  like the Voice key, does nothing while its panel cannot be seen.

- 2026-10-20: the default Clackatoo colours now follow the phone instead of being
  fixed Tokyo Night: the system's role colours (Android 14+), the nearest system
  tones (Android 12-13) or a fallback table (below Android 12), in the phone's
  dark or light theme, for day and night alike. The keyboard rebuilds its views
  when those colours change. Key labels are Inter (Regular; Medium where
  HeliBoard uses bold) instead of JetBrains Mono, which is removed with its
  licence file. Keys have a one-pixel hairline edge; the pressed key, the Enter
  key, the selected suggestion and the voice/Check panel's main button use the
  accent. Round shapes of the suggestion strip, the more-suggestions divider, the
  pinned toolbar key glow and the keyboard's own toast are square (6dp or 4dp).
  New files: `clackatoo/ClackatooPalette.kt`, `third_party/inter/`,
  `assets/fonts/Inter-*.ttf`, a few `*_clackatoo` drawables. Small hooks were added
  to `DefaultColors` (optional parameters; other themes are unchanged),
  `KeyboardSwitcher`, `KeyboardTypeface`, `SuggestionStripView` and
  `MoreSuggestions`.
- 2026-10-27: NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 as a second speech engine, with live
  text: while the user speaks, the voice panel shows the words recognised so
  far (the text goes into the field after Stop, as before). Parakeet runs in
  the isolated model process through parakeet.cpp, built in a new Gradle
  module `asr` with its own static, hidden ggml; Silero VAD (shipped in the
  APK, `assets/models/ggml-silero-v6.2.0.bin`, loaded by whisper.cpp) cuts the
  audio into utterances. Whisper stays the engine when Parakeet is not
  installed. New files: `asr/`, `LiveSegmenter.kt`, `LiveSession.kt`; hooks in
  `MlService`, `MlClient`, `AssistController`, `AssistPanelView`,
  `AudioRecorder`, `ModelCatalog`, `ModelStore`, `DebugWavReceiver`, the Voice
  typing settings screen and the `ml` module (voice-activity detection).
- 2026-10-28: one-tap model downloads and a choice of models. A new Android
  application, "Clackatoo Models" (module `models`, application id
  `io.github.highlyproteus.clackatoo.models`), is the only part with the INTERNET
  permission: the keyboard asks it, through a signature permission, to download
  one model of a built-in list by id; it downloads the pinned file from Hugging
  Face, checks size and SHA-256 and hands it over as a read-only file descriptor,
  and the keyboard checks it again and installs it as before (the keyboard still has
  no INTERNET permission). The list of models is a new shared module `catalog`
  (nine more models than before, each pinned by size and SHA-256), the keyboard
  has a choice of model per role (`ModelChoice`), and the Voice and Check keys offer
  to download the recommended models in the panel when none is installed. New
  files: `catalog/`, `models/`, the package `helium314.keyboard.clackatoo.models`,
  `res/values/strings-clackatoo-models.xml`; hooks in `ModelCatalog`,
  `ModelStore`, `AssistController`, `AssistPanelView`, `DebugWavReceiver`, `App`,
  the Voice typing and Grammar check settings screens and the manifest (a
  signature permission, a receiver service, a package query). The release
  workflow builds and signs both APKs.
- 2026-10-22: the keyboard data stays in credential-protected storage when the
  app is preinstalled as a system app (only the input method service is
  direct-boot aware); clipboard history skips clips marked sensitive and is
  excluded from backups; the extracted-dictionary cleanup after an upgrade waits
  until the user has unlocked; native code is built with -ffile-prefix-map for
  reproducible builds.
- 2026-10-27: named Clackatoo: application id `io.github.highlyproteus.clackatoo`
  (debug builds: `.debug` suffix, label "Clackatoo debug"), app, input method,
  spell checker and settings labels "Clackatoo" in every language, new launcher
  icon (a cockatoo keycap), the About screen's source and licence links point to
  https://github.com/highlyproteus/clackatoo, version 1.0.0. GitHub workflows
  replaced (unit tests; signed releases), HeliBoard's issue, discussion and
  pull-request templates removed, HeliBoard's CONTRIBUTING.md and AI_USAGE.md
  moved to docs/.
- 2026-10-27: added swipe typing without any closed-source library. HeliBoard's
  native engine already captured strokes and computed per-point key
  probabilities; only the decoder that turns them into words came from Google's
  proprietary library. Clackatoo has its own, new Apache-2.0 decoder in
  `app/src/main/jni/src/suggest/policyimpl/gesture/`, replacing the factory hook
  for the library; `JniUtils` no longer tries to load `libjni_latinimegoogle.so`;
  the gesture settings no longer offer the (unsupported) space-aware option. The
  engine also builds on a host for testing (`tools/gesture-eval/`, never shipped;
  small additive changes to `ProximityInfo`, `Dictionary` and `SuggestionResults`
  for that, a larger node cache for gestures in `DicNodesCache`, and `Suggest`
  continues a search only when nodes were cached). HeliBoard's gesture data
  gathering stays hidden and off (`GestureDataPolicy`).
- 2026-10-27: redesigned the settings. Every settings screen, dialog and the
  set-up wizard now use shared Material 3 components (grouped panels with the
  default 12dp medium shape, rows with a state subtitle, M3 default dialogs);
  the new home screen shows a status or set-up card and groups Typing, Voice
  & writing and Look & feel with live state rows; the settings window shows
  the wallpaper behind a tinted scrim (blurred on Android 12+ when the phone
  allows it) with translucent panels, and the new switch "Glass background"
  turns it off for solid surfaces. The settings activity theme is translucent
  (`platformActivityTheme.Settings`). New files: the package
  `helium314.keyboard.clackatoo.ui`, `res/values/strings-clackatoo-settings.xml`.
  Changed: `SearchScreen`, `Preference`, `Theme`, `SettingsActivity`,
  `SettingsNavHost`, `MainSettingsScreen`, `WelcomeWizard`,
  `ThreeButtonAlertDialog` and the rows of the language, dictionary, personal
  dictionary, colour and subtype screens. The Voice typing and Grammar check
  screens show each model as a card (neutral icon, maker as text, size, radio
  choice per role, Download / progress and Cancel / Ready with a delete menu,
  "Get Clackatoo Models" when the companion app is missing) on the
  `ModelDownloads` and `ModelChoice` API; "Import model file" stays. The first
  model of a fresh install is no longer refused for "not enough storage"
  (`ModelStore` checked the free space of a folder that did not exist yet).
  No preference key changed. The Material 3 default shapes replace the square
  6dp/4dp design rule.
- 2026-10-27: keyboard themes. Keys, key-like buttons and the strip's buttons
  have 8dp corners (they were 6dp), the keyboard's own panels 12dp (Material 3
  shapes instead of "square, not pills"). New "Glass" colour themes (`glass`
  follows the phone's colours and dark mode, `glass_dark`, `glass_light`): the
  keyboard window is translucent and, where Android blurs windows
  (`WindowManager.isCrossWindowBlurEnabled`, Android 12+), what is behind the
  keyboard is blurred by a small window behind the keyboard window; elsewhere
  the tint is nearly opaque. Labels keep 4.5:1 over white and over black. 23
  colour themes of Omarchy (MIT, https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy, colours
  only, commit 600ca886632d4e0e2bba5afb759b3bb8d382cddc) generated by
  `tools/omarchy-themes/generate.py` into `OmarchyThemeData.kt`, with labels
  raised to 4.5:1 where a theme is fainter. A new theme picker (Settings >
  Appearance > Theme) shows every theme as a live miniature, grouped as Follow
  phone, Glass, Omarchy, Classic and Custom, with separate day and night
  choices; the theme preferences are the same as before, so existing choices and
  custom themes are unchanged. New files: `clackatoo/GlassPalette.kt`,
  `GlassWindow.kt`, `OmarchyThemes.kt`, `OmarchyThemeData.kt`,
  `ThemeCatalog.kt`, `settings/screens/ThemePickerScreen.kt`,
  `third_party/omarchy/`, `tools/omarchy-themes/`. Small hooks were added to
  `ClackatooPalette` (translucent colours, popup colour), `ClackatooStyle`,
  `KeyboardTheme`, `DefaultColors` and `Colors` (translucent window, blur
  radius; the strip is transparent on a translucent keyboard), `LatinIME`
  (window set-up and blur), the Appearance screen and the settings navigation.
- 2026-10-28: Glass keyboard redesign. The clear parts of the keyboard (gaps
  between keys, edges) are now a light tint (about 26%, 86% where the phone
  cannot blur) and everything that carries text or icons has a frosted
  backing (about 78% opaque with a hairline): keys, every suggestion, toolbar
  key and emoji tab of the strip (a backing of its own each, no longer one
  tint under the whole strip), the clipboard's placeholder, the strip under
  the system's navigation icons and the text of the voice and check panel,
  which is now clear glass instead of a solid panel. Popups stay solid (also
  the Enter key's popup). The theme picker says whether the phone blurs
  windows. New file `clackatoo/GlassBacking.kt`; `ClackatooPalette` (backing,
  contrast checked over white, black, grey and saturated backdrops),
  `GlassPalette`, `GlassWindow`, `Colors` and `DefaultColors` (backing),
  `SuggestionStripView`, `EmojiPalettesView`, `ClipboardHistoryView` and
  `AssistPanelView` were changed.
- 2026-10-28: models are offered for download only where their native code
  ships (64-bit ARM or x86_64, Android 9 or newer); elsewhere the cards read
  "Not available on this phone" and the Voice and Check keys say why
  (`ModelChoice.runsHere`, `MissingModels`).
- 2026-10-28: clearer glass settings. The window is lightly tinted (heavier
  where the phone does not blur), the panels are lighter frosted glass, and the
  page title, section headers, hints and toolbar icons sit on small frosted
  backings instead of the bare window; dialogs are frosted over a blurred
  settings screen on phones that blur. `GlassStyle`, `GlassWindow`,
  `SettingsComponents`, `SearchScreen`, `SettingsActivity` and
  `ThreeButtonAlertDialog` changed; `GlassStyleTest` checks every text surface.
- 2026-10-28: one model per role is suggested for the phone ("Suggested for this
  phone", shown first and offered by the "needs a model" sheet) from its memory,
  CPU features and keyboard languages (`DeviceProfile`, `ModelSuggestions`,
  numbers measured in ml/README.md).
- 2026-10-28: experimental custom models. Settings > Voice typing and Grammar
  check can import any model file the format detection recognises (Whisper
  ggml, Parakeet GGUF, text GGUF), and the Clackatoo Models app has a "Browse
  Hugging Face" screen for them; the keyboard checks size, format and a test
  load, runs them only in the isolated process, keeps them apart and marks them
  experimental (`CustomModels.kt`, `ModelStore.importCustom`, the receiver's
  `TX_CUSTOM_HANDOVER`, `MSG_PROBE` and chat-template prompting in `ml`). Models
  the user adds have their own licences, which Clackatoo does not list.
- 2026-10-28: voice typing opens the microphone only after the recording panel
  is on screen: the Voice key shows the panel and the start waits for its first
  layout (a start that cannot show the panel within 1 s is cancelled with the
  microphone still closed), which also fixes a start that was silently cancelled
  on a keyboard that had just started (`AssistController.startListening`); the
  model process keeps only the models of the current use in memory
  (`ModelResidency`).
- 2026-10-28: new settings home screen. A header with the app icon and a search
  button, a field to try the keyboard in (it asks the keyboard not to learn
  from it and is emptied when you leave) with Theme, Voice and Languages
  buttons, a setup checklist with one-tap model downloads while a model is
  missing, tiles for swipe typing, voice typing, grammar check and languages,
  four live theme swatches that apply a theme, and a "More settings" list that
  keeps every screen reachable (`HomeScreen`, `HomeComponents`,
  `SetupChecklist`, `ThemeSelection`, `ThemeMiniature`, `SearchScreen`).
- 2026-10-28: key vibration and key sounds are on by default
  (`Defaults.PREF_VIBRATE_ON` and `PREF_SOUND_ON` are true; HeliBoard has both
  off). Existing choices are kept: a saved setting always wins over the default.
- 2026-10-28: stable download links and a download page. Each release also
  carries byte-identical version-less copies (`clackatoo.apk`,
  `clackatoo-models.apk`) so that `releases/latest/download/clackatoo.apk`
  always works, and `site/` (published to GitHub Pages by the Pages workflow,
  checked by `tools/check-site`) is a static download page with no scripts or
  third-party resources. It contains the Obtainium "Get it on Obtainium" badge
  (`site/assets/badge_obtainium.png`, `docs/badge-obtainium.png`; from
  https://github.com/ImranR98/Obtainium, GPL-3.0) and screenshots from
  `docs/screenshots/`.
- 2026-10-29: clearer privacy wording in the settings: the home subtitle reads
  "Private keyboard with no internet access" and the Voice typing summary says
  speech is turned into text on the phone and the recording never leaves it
  (instead of "everything stays on your phone", which could be read as covering
  messages the user sends).
- 2026-10-29: model downloads keep the keyboard's binding until its foreground
  start is accepted, avoiding a competing companion self-start that could crash
  Clackatoo Models and leave progress at zero. Downloads remain started when
  settings is closed. Idle teardown is serialised with request admission so an
  ending download cannot remove a newer one's foreground state. An idle-stopped
  service kept alive by a binding can accept the next download; requests
  rejected during destruction are refunded rather than left queued indefinitely.
- 2026-10-29: added a shared privacy policy for Clackatoo and Clackatoo Models
  to the static site, linked from the download page and README. Both apps expose
  the policy in their settings/main screen via an external browser; the keyboard
  entry is searchable and no network permission was added.
- 2026-10-29: the English clean-up can be switched off where it is used. The
  voice panel shows a "Clean-up on/off" toggle while recording (English, with a
  clean-up model installed), which flips the same setting as Settings > Voice
  typing, where the switch now heads the Clean-up section and hides the writing
  style while off. With clean-up off, the needs-a-model sheet no longer offers
  the clean-up model.
- 2026-10-29: voice typing keeps the screen on while it records and transcribes,
  and asks "Discard this dictation?" (Discard / Keep) before Cancel, Back, swiping
  the toolbar down or a toolbar key throws a dictation away; the key runs after
  Discard. The microphone stays on while the question shows in the recording
  panel; a recording or transcript that finishes meanwhile is inserted only on
  Keep. Added CONTRIBUTING.md.

